.TH "RECORD\-UPDATE\.PY" "" "May 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-update\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-update\.py \-\-table=\fR\fITableName\fR \fB\-\-\fR\fIcolumn_name\fR\fB=\fR\fIvalue\fR [\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-update\.py\fR inserts or updates a single record in the RECORD provenance database from the command line\. It is the primary write helper used by \fBrecord\.sh\fR to record provenance entities such as applications, processes, boxes, persons, and pipelines\.
.P
The script takes a mandatory \fB\-\-table\fR argument identifying the entity class to operate on, followed by one or more \fB\-\-column=value\fR arguments supplying field values\. Column names are matched case\-insensitively against the attributes of the named entity class\.
.P
\fBrecord\-update\.py\fR first attempts to insert the record by calling \fBadd\fR\. If the record already exists (detected via a backend\-appropriate uniqueness exception \(em \fBGremlinVertexExists\fR, \fBsqlite3\.IntegrityError\fR, or \fBpsycopg2\.errors\.UniqueViolation\fR) it falls back to calling \fBupdate\fR on the same object instead\. Any other exception is reported to standard error and the script exits with a non\-zero status\.
.P
On success the primary key value of the inserted or updated record is printed to standard output\. If the primary key is composite, the component values are printed as a comma\-separated list\. This output is captured by \fBrecord\.sh\fR to chain identifiers between successive \fBrecord\-update\.py\fR calls\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-table=\fR\fITableName\fR
Required\. The entity class to insert or update\. \fITableName\fR is case\-sensitive and must match a class defined in \fBrecord\.py\fR exactly (for example \fBApplication\fR, \fBBox\fR, \fBProcess\fR, \fBPerson\fR, \fBPipeline\fR)\.
.TP
\fB\-\-\fR\fIcolumn_name\fR\fB=\fR\fIvalue\fR
Sets the field \fIcolumn_name\fR to \fIvalue\fR\. Column names are matched case\-insensitively\. At least one column argument must be supplied\. Any argument that does not match a column defined on the entity class raises an \fBIllegalArgumentError\fR and the script exits without writing to the database\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the \fB\-\-table\fR argument is missing or names an unknown class;
.IP "\(bu" 4
no valid column arguments are supplied;
.IP "\(bu" 4
a column name does not exist on the named entity class;
.IP "\(bu" 4
a database error other than a uniqueness violation occurs during \fBadd\fR; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
the fallback \fBupdate\fR call raises an exception\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBrecord\fR library\. Refer to \fBrecord\.py\fR for the full list, including:
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Selects the database backend\. One of \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBpostgres\fR, or \fBgremlin\fR\. The appropriate uniqueness exception type is selected at import time based on this variable\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBFILE\fR
Path to the SQLite database file\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBUSER\fR
PostgreSQL username\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBNAME\fR
PostgreSQL database name\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_HOST\fR
PostgreSQL hostname\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PORT\fR
PostgreSQL port number\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD\fR
PostgreSQL password\. Required when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_HOST\fR
WebSocket URL of the Gremlin server\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR
Per\-query evaluation timeout in milliseconds\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Prints the primary key value of the affected record to standard output on success\. For composite primary keys the component values are printed as a comma\-separated list, with quoting and the SQL \fBAND\fR clauses stripped\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Register a computer node:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-update\.py \e
    \-\-table=Computer \e
    \-\-id_computer=computer_myhost \e
    \-\-name=myhost \e
    \-\-ip_address=192\.168\.1\.1
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Register or update an application, capturing its ID:
.IP "" 4
.nf
id_app=$(record\-update\.py \e
    \-\-table=Application \e
    \-\-id_application=application_12345 \e
    \-\-name=my_sim \e
    \-\-language=Python)
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Register a process start, then update it with an end time:
.IP "" 4
.nf
id_process=$(record\-update\.py \e
    \-\-table=Process \e
    \-\-id_process=process_abc \e
    \-\-executable="$id_app" \e
    \-\-start_time=20240101T120000)

record\-update\.py \e
    \-\-table=Process \e
    \-\-id_process=process_abc \e
    \-\-executable="$id_app" \e
    \-\-end_time=20240101T130000
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/record\.py\fR
The RECORD provenance library\. Must be importable as \fBrecord\fR; the script appends no path prefix, so \fBrecord\.py\fR must be on \fBsys\.path\fR or in the same directory\.
