.SH "BUGS"
The \fBtable_parameter\fR regex will raise an \fBAttributeError\fR rather than skipping gracefully if any argument in \fBsys\.argv\fR does not match the \fB\-\-table=\fR pattern, because \fBre\.match\fR returns \fBNone\fR for non\-matching strings and \fBNone\.groups()\fR is called unconditionally\. The same issue affects \fBcolumn_parameter\.match(arg)\fR in the column\-parsing loop\.
.P
Debug output is unconditionally enabled by the line \fBrecord\.debug = True\fR at module level and cannot be suppressed via the \fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR environment variable\.
.P
The variable declared as \fBcolums\fR (a typo for \fBcolumns\fR) on line 89 is unused; the actual \fBcolumns\fR dictionary is assigned by \fBparameters\fR on the next line\.
.P
The primary key output is derived by applying three successive regex substitutions to the SQL \fBWHERE\fR clause fragment returned by \fBgetPrimaryKeys\fR\. This approach is fragile: primary key values that contain the literal string ` AND ` or a leading \fB=\fR may be mangled in the output\.
.P
The bare \fBexcept: raise\fR in the \fBupdate\fR fallback swallows the original exception context, making it harder to diagnose failures that occur during the update path\.
